From: Project Arctic
Subject: user32: SwitchToThisWindow gives the foreground before it restores.

The taskbar and Alt+Tab switch with it. A minimized window was restored
first, in its own thread and synchronously: a game takes its time there
(CS2 sets its display mode), and the mouse moving over another program
meanwhile made that one the program the user last touched, so the
foreground the shell gave next was refused. CS2 came back restored but
inactive, DXVK gave the desktop its mode back, and the game stood still
for eight seconds until it took the foreground itself (2026-11-18). The
foreground goes first now, while the click on the taskbar still counts.
---
diff --git a/dlls/user32/win.c b/dlls/user32/win.c
index ac460b3..f534418 100644
--- a/dlls/user32/win.c
+++ b/dlls/user32/win.c
@@ -669,9 +669,11 @@ void WINAPI SwitchToThisWindow( HWND hwnd, BOOL alt_tab )
 {
     arctic_log_stack( IsIconic( hwnd ) ? "activate: SwitchToThisWindow, restoring" : "activate: SwitchToThisWindow",
                       hwnd, alt_tab );
-    /* as in Windows, the window becomes the foreground one, not only the top one */
-    if (IsIconic( hwnd )) NtUserShowWindow( hwnd, SW_RESTORE );
+    /* as in Windows, the window becomes the foreground one, not only the top
+     * one; first, while the user's click still gives the caller the right:
+     * the restore runs in the window's thread and may take long */
     NtUserSetForegroundWindow( hwnd );
+    if (IsIconic( hwnd )) NtUserShowWindow( hwnd, SW_RESTORE );
 }
 
 
